{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the omitted lanes repair at head 5cc4b4c1, tree c9ff6411, for request ca74f78b and review request dc233b17. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nI reviewed the diff from 6a5b87d4. My report a6787cf0 stands for everything else on this head.\n\n## The changes I requested\n\n- The Work card now names its omission and offers no scope. `lanesLeft` returns the first-lanes sentence for `work`, after the check for no omission, so a card with nothing omitted says nothing. The check applies on both the row and no-row paths.\n- `work`'s tool answer has no `next`, on the normal answer and on `rows-output-limit`. `needs_you` and `since` keep it.\n- `docs/mcp.md` and the README say that a null `next` ends the walk, and that a lane opened during it appears on the next walk.\n- The nine-lane case now asserts that the first window keeps its marks after the second mark.\n\n## The first gate\n\nThe first gate at this head exited 1 with `EnvironmentTeardownError`, and I accept your account as enough. The second gate at the same head and tree exits 0. Nothing on this head touches `lending.scope.test.ts`. The same error text also appears in `test.log` of at least six earlier gate runs, for example under `2026-10-27-br7-current-names` and `2026-10-30-room-proof-reuse-repair`, so this head didn't introduce it. I didn't check how those runs ended. The cause stays unknown, and it costs a rerun when it happens. If you want it gone, it needs its own request.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The gate at 1f220d10, tree 1ce92ac6, exits 0: Plain 3,218 with one skip, Native 900 with two skips. It includes main 074255e8, which settles my point about the merge. From there to this head, only the note and the manifest change.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree` of 074255e8 and this head gives this head's tree.\n- The evidence verifies. All 16 manifest rows match, the directory holds 53 files with none writable, and `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean with digest 92fd2a8c.\n- All ten control logs say that they distinguish, and each now names its assertion. They ran at dd41e4e6, and C4 ran again at 1f220d10, where the only change is that assertion's message. The named assertions match the note's table, so C4 and C6, and C5 and C7, are no longer identical. I read the logs and did not rerun them.\n- I ran `s4.test.mjs` and `decision.test.mjs` once, 12 of 12. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` finds 775 links with 0 broken, `check-commit-messages` checks 11 with 0 flagged, and the worktree stayed clean.\n\nNo Worker or real room has run this. No independent second read ran on this repair.\n\n## For the planner\n\nTwo limits in the note have no open request: a room over 62 lanes reaches `full` in the mark store, and rows beyond a window's 50-row or byte limit are unreachable, with a `rows-output-limit` error showing as `unavailable` on the card. Neither matters at this room's size. The note says so, and you can leave them until a real room nears them.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved. The stateless cursor keeps `since` a pure read, and `work` stays a first-window read.\n- Security: approved. No authority widens, and a mark stays local and bound to displayed heads.\n- Simplification: approved. `walks` is one flag on one private function.\n- Deployment: none now. The planner deploys this after J4 closes.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:02254b68eae9f1c555be6712fe086f7778deffa9","binding":"assigned","head":"5cc4b4c1fc560b09b1b35367217048ec5881c5d0","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e46d3fff27b1e3935dd302e97790526ed62d51d2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:04996c9877bd69fd490cf0d517f1d22c88fbd99a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e46d3fff27b1e3935dd302e97790526ed62d51d2","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sh